<speak>It has been quite a busy week, actually. My brother used to handle most of the warehouse coordination, but now he is stepping back from the everyday running. My nephew is taking on more, although he still comes to me whenever two people give him different answers. I do not mind helping, but the interruptions are constant. One moment I am looking at a delivery schedule, the next somebody wants me to settle an argument about where the stationery should be kept. A family business can be like that. Even the small decisions somehow find their way back to the same few people.</speak>